|* Post-layout ro_ring5 with the shared substrate floating and only ONE ring
|* running -- the control that separates capacitive LOADING from inter-ring
|* COUPLING.
|*
|* Purpose (issue #22, acceptance criterion 4). The sibling deck
|* tb_post_layout_substrate_float.spice runs all four post-layout rings with
|* the extracted substrate node `vsubs` left floating, and its slowest ring
|* (wstv = 0.42 um) comes out measurably FASTER than in the hard-tied deck.
|* Two different mechanisms could produce that, and they mean opposite
|* things:
|*
|*   LOADING  -- a floating `vsubs` is not a ground. Every net-to-substrate
|*               capacitance stops being a capacitance to ground and becomes
|*               part of a series network between nets, so each net's own
|*               effective load falls and EVERY ring speeds up a little.
|*               This is an artifact of the unmodelled substrate tie, not a
|*               statement about ring independence.
|*   COUPLING -- the four rings share one node, so each ring's switching
|*               current is injected into every other ring, pulling their
|*               frequencies toward each other. THIS is the quantity
|*               DR-0003 section 8 flags as unmeasured and entropy-relevant.
|*
|* This deck holds rings 2/3/4 at en = 0 while leaving them physically
|* present -- same instances, same extracted capacitance on the shared node,
|* simply not switching. Ring 1's period here is therefore its
|* floating-substrate period with the LOADING mechanism fully present and
|* the COUPLING mechanism removed. Differencing the three decks at the same
|* corner separates them:
|*
|*   loading  = t(this deck)                 - t(hard-tied, 4 running)
|*   coupling = t(float deck, 4 running)     - t(this deck)
|*
|* Without this control the float deck's numbers cannot be attributed, and
|* an attribution is exactly what DR-0003 section 8 asks for.
|*
|* Topology: identical to tb_post_layout_substrate_float.spice -- four
|* post-layout rings, wstv = 0.42/0.44/0.46/0.48 um, one physical layout
|* cell per ring, each on its own supply, `vsubs` untied -- except that
|* Venp2/Venp3/Venp4 sit at 0 V instead of 1.98. Ring 1's measurements
|* are named identically to the float deck's so the two records difference
|* line for line.
|*
|* This file is a TEMPLATE: sim/bin/corner-run.py substitutes /Users/rwalters/.volare/volare/sky130/versions/c6d73a35f524070e85faff4a6a9eef49553ebc2b/sky130A/libs.tech/combined/sky130.lib.spice,
|* tt, /Users/rwalters/GitHub/sky130-trng/.loom/worktrees/issue-22/layout/pex/ro_ring5_pex.spice, -40.0, 1.98 and 5p. As committed it
|* is not a runnable deck.
|
|.option scale=1u
|.lib "/Users/rwalters/.volare/volare/sky130/versions/c6d73a35f524070e85faff4a6a9eef49553ebc2b/sky130A/libs.tech/combined/sky130.lib.spice" tt
|
|* post-layout subcircuit library only (see header)
|.include "/Users/rwalters/GitHub/sky130-trng/.loom/worktrees/issue-22/layout/pex/ro_ring5_pex.spice"
|
|.temp -40.0
|
|* NOTE: no `Vsub vsubs 0` tie here -- that is the entire difference from
|* tb_post_layout_ro_ring5.spice. See the header.
|
|Vddrp1 vddrp1 0 dc 1.98
|Venp1 enp1 0 dc 1.98
|xgp1 p1o enp1 p1a vddrp1 0 ro_nand2_pex_wstv0p42
|x1p1 p1a p1b vddrp1 0 ro_stage_pex_wstv0p42
|x2p1 p1b p1c vddrp1 0 ro_stage_pex_wstv0p42
|x3p1 p1c p1d vddrp1 0 ro_stage_pex_wstv0p42
|x4p1 p1d p1o vddrp1 0 ro_stage_pex_wstv0p42
|
|* rings 2/3/4: physically present (their extracted capacitance still loads
|* the shared substrate node) but held stopped -- see the header.
|Vddrp2 vddrp2 0 dc 1.98
|Venp2 enp2 0 dc 0
|xgp2 p2o enp2 p2a vddrp2 0 ro_nand2_pex_wstv0p44
|x1p2 p2a p2b vddrp2 0 ro_stage_pex_wstv0p44
|x2p2 p2b p2c vddrp2 0 ro_stage_pex_wstv0p44
|x3p2 p2c p2d vddrp2 0 ro_stage_pex_wstv0p44
|x4p2 p2d p2o vddrp2 0 ro_stage_pex_wstv0p44
|
|Vddrp3 vddrp3 0 dc 1.98
|Venp3 enp3 0 dc 0
|xgp3 p3o enp3 p3a vddrp3 0 ro_nand2_pex_wstv0p46
|x1p3 p3a p3b vddrp3 0 ro_stage_pex_wstv0p46
|x2p3 p3b p3c vddrp3 0 ro_stage_pex_wstv0p46
|x3p3 p3c p3d vddrp3 0 ro_stage_pex_wstv0p46
|x4p3 p3d p3o vddrp3 0 ro_stage_pex_wstv0p46
|
|Vddrp4 vddrp4 0 dc 1.98
|Venp4 enp4 0 dc 0
|xgp4 p4o enp4 p4a vddrp4 0 ro_nand2_pex_wstv0p48
|x1p4 p4a p4b vddrp4 0 ro_stage_pex_wstv0p48
|x2p4 p4b p4c vddrp4 0 ro_stage_pex_wstv0p48
|x3p4 p4c p4d vddrp4 0 ro_stage_pex_wstv0p48
|x4p4 p4d p4o vddrp4 0 ro_stage_pex_wstv0p48
|
|* --- output buffers, one per ring, on a shared block supply ------------
|* Present so this deck's loading matches tb_post_layout_ro_ring5.spice's
|* exactly -- the whole point of this deck is to difference against that
|* one, which is only meaningful if the two rings are equally loaded.
|Vddp vddp 0 dc 1.98
|xbp1 p1o p1ob vddp 0 ro_buf_pex
|xbp2 p2o p2ob vddp 0 ro_buf_pex
|xbp3 p3o p3ob vddp 0 ro_buf_pex
|xbp4 p4o p4ob vddp 0 ro_buf_pex
|
|.ic v(p1o)=0 v(p1a)=1.98 v(p1b)=0 v(p1c)=1.98 v(p1d)=0
|.ic v(p2o)=0 v(p2a)=1.98 v(p2b)=0 v(p2c)=1.98 v(p2d)=0
|.ic v(p3o)=0 v(p3a)=1.98 v(p3b)=0 v(p3c)=1.98 v(p3d)=0
|.ic v(p4o)=0 v(p4a)=1.98 v(p4b)=0 v(p4c)=1.98 v(p4d)=0
|.ic v(vsubs)=0
|
|.tran 5p 160n uic
|
|.control
|run
|
|meas tran tp1a when v(p1o)=0.5*1.98 rise=3
|meas tran tp1b when v(p1o)=0.5*1.98 rise=11
|let t_solo_wstv0p42 = (tp1b - tp1a)/8
|* No ladder span here: rings 2/3/4 are stopped, so there is no ladder.
|
|* How hard is ONE ring driving the shared node? Compare against the float
|* deck's own vsubs_pp, where four rings drive it.
|meas tran vsubmax MAX v(vsubs) from=20n to=160n
|meas tran vsubmin MIN v(vsubs) from=20n to=160n
|let vsubs_pp_solo = vsubmax - vsubmin
|let vsubs_pp_solo_frac = (vsubmax - vsubmin) / 1.98
|
|* Ring-node swing on the one running ring, to confirm it is still running
|* normally with its three stopped neighbours' capacitance on the node.
|meas tran vmaxp1 MAX v(p1o) from=20n to=160n
|meas tran vminp1 MIN v(p1o) from=20n to=160n
|let swing_frac_solo_wstv0p42 = (vmaxp1 - vminp1) / 1.98
|
|print t_solo_wstv0p42
|print vsubs_pp_solo
|print vsubs_pp_solo_frac
|print swing_frac_solo_wstv0p42
|.endc
|.end
|

